<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!-- Release config: cleartext is never permitted. Debug builds override this
     file (src/debug/res/xml) to allow cleartext to the emulator loopback only.
     Build types do not merge resources into one another, so the debug override
     replaces this file wholesale in the debug APK and cannot reach the release
     one. This config also takes precedence over `usesCleartextTraffic` in the
     manifest from API 24 up — see the comment above <application> there.

     No `trust-anchors` block, deliberately. A `base-config` that omits one
     inherits the platform default, and for targetSdk 24+ that default is
     system CAs only: user-installed certificates are already not trusted, in
     debug as well as release, because there is no `debug-overrides` block
     either. Writing the anchors out would restate the platform default and
     invite someone to "just add the user source" while they are in here.

     NO CERTIFICATE PINNING, and that is a decision rather than an omission.
     Pinning defends against a trusted-CA compromise or a corporate MITM
     proxy; the exposure it adds is that every pinned certificate is a fuse on
     a timer, and this app cannot rotate one. The pin would live in an APK on
     the user's device, so a certificate rotation the server does routinely —
     an expiry, an ACME renewal onto a new intermediate, a CDN provider change
     — bricks every installed copy of the app until a store release ships AND
     each user updates, which is days, not minutes, and the users who never
     update are simply gone. The traffic is already TLS-only to a single
     first-party origin over the system trust store, which is the industry
     bar; pinning would trade a residual risk for a self-inflicted outage we
     have no lever to shorten.

     If this is ever revisited, the prerequisites are a backup pin for the
     next key already published, a monitored expiry, and a server-driven kill
     switch — not just a `<pin-set>` block. -->
<network-security-config>
    <base-config cleartextTrafficPermitted="false" />
</network-security-config>
